                "reply_count": 1,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter Web Client",
                "text": "U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP) officers are on the front lines every day to ensure our nation's borders are safe and secure. To help them effectively protect our communities, we have a responsibility to ensure mental health resources and additional support is available.  \n\nThat's why I supported the passage of H.R. 3965, Providing Emotional Assistance with Relief and Love Act (PEARL Act), to create a pilot program allowing CBP officers to adopt dogs from local shelters to be trained as support dogs.",
